#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Tessera's release builder (the build half): builds the ready-made
tessera-ui (and tessera-events) that tools/native-install.py downloads, in
place of the build job of .github/workflows/tessera-ui.yml (which can't run
while the account's Actions are locked). Runs on server1 from a systemd user
timer every 10 minutes. It never signs and never publishes: there's no key
here. The user's laptop picks up each finished set with
tools/release-builder/publish-release, checks it, signs it and publishes it
(docs/releases.md, "The release builder").

    tessera-release                     everything that has no build yet (main, beta, v* tags)
    tessera-release --branch beta       that branch only (repeatable; no tags)
    tessera-release --build-only        build and pack; no ready set
    tessera-release --status            the status JSON
    tessera-release --list-ready        the sets waiting for the laptop (JSON)
    tessera-release --health            those and the status, in one answer (the laptop's 2-minute look)
    tessera-release --mark-published TAG TREE   the laptop published that set

What it builds: main (the Stable channel's rolling release tessera-ui-latest),
beta (tessera-ui-beta) and every v* tag (its own release), fetched from GitHub
(https, public) into a clean clone of its own (~/tessera-release/src). A build
is named by the git tree of native/ (git rev-parse <commit>:native); nothing
to do when that release already has the tree's manifest (GitHub, asked
anonymously), or a set for it is ready or published here. A commit without
tools/tessera-ui.pub is skipped (nothing built from it could be checked).
Otherwise: both variants exactly like CI (cargo build --release --locked: the
full release profile, LTO and one codegen unit; RUSTFLAGS
"-C target-cpu=x86-64-v3" and ""), through ~/bin/tbuild (a cgroup scope with
low CPU/IO weight: the machine's own work comes first), packed with the
manifest exactly like CI. tessera-ui is told what it is (build_env:
TESSERA_BUILD_CHANNEL, _VARIANT, _KIND=release, _COMMIT, _DATE; its build.rs),
so `tessera-ui --version` reads e.g. "tessera-ui 0.1.0 (stable, 7baa48d,
2026-11-17, x86-64-v3, release build)" and the manifest records that line. The set lands in
~/tessera-release/out/<release tag>/<tree>/ (both archives and the manifest)
with a READY file (JSON: what it is, and each file's size and sha256), written
last. The laptop's --mark-published renames READY to PUBLISHED.

Built variants are kept per tree and channel in
~/tessera-release/built/<tree>-<channel> (the newest six), so a tree built
again for the same channel is only packed again. Channels never share one:
tessera-ui carries its channel, commit and date (build_env), and a beta
set packed from a build made for main said "Stable" (and patches were made
from programs beta installs never had; audit #725). A tree promoted from
beta to main is built again for main.

Tested before it's offered: each variant is installed in a hidden sandbox
arena here (tools/release-builder/pretest.sh, installed as
~/bin/tessera-pretest) and must start, answer IPC within 30 s, draw, and lock
and unlock. A variant that fails isn't made ready; the reason is in the log
and the status (the laptop's publisher says so in a notification).
TESSERA_RELEASE_NO_PRETEST=1 skips it (tests).

Patches: each set also carries zstd --patch-from patches from the last three
published builds of the same release (built/<tree>-<channel> keeps their archives) to
this one, per variant and program (a program that didn't change gets none:
an install keeps it). The manifest lists each (file, size, sha256 and the
sha256 of the program it starts from); the laptop signs them like the rest,
and tools/native-install.py downloads the patch when it has the program it
starts from, checking the patch's signature and checksum and the rebuilt
program's checksum against the manifest. Patches are named for their build
(tessera-ui-<tree>-…), so a rolling release's pruning of a build takes its
patches with it.

Profiles: beta builds with the "local" cargo profile (thin LTO, 16 codegen
units: minutes), stable and tags with the full release profile (LTO, one
codegen unit: about 45 minutes); a tree built for beta is built again with
the release profile before it's packed for main. mold links when it's
installed. Both variants build at once only with MemTotal of 24 GB or more
(two release links at once need about that); otherwise one after the other.

Bundles (tools/tessera-bundle.py, docs/releases.md "Bundles"): for every
commit of main, beta and each tag (not only a new native/ tree), one bundle
per variant: the commit's files (less native/, site/, tests/), its built
shaders and native helpers, the glass plugin built here against the
Hyprland installed here, both programs (from built/<tree>), and one
manifest (tessera-<commit>.bundle.json: every file's sha256, both archives,
the package lock from this machine's pacman: the Hyprland family and
Quickshell exactly, the rest minimums). It's made with that commit's own
tools/tessera-bundle.py (a commit without it gets none), in
out/<release>/<commit>/ with a READY whose "type" is "bundle"; the laptop
signs and publishes it like the program sets, and for a rolling release
also as tessera-latest.bundle.json (the channel's pointer). Its parts need
Hyprland's headers, qt6-shadertools, cmake and Qt's development files here;
build them in a plain Arch system (the lock's versions are what installs
fetch from the Arch Linux Archive). TESSERA_RELEASE_NO_BUNDLE=1 skips them.

Started the moment a branch is pushed by tools/push-release (it pokes this
service over ssh); the 10-minute timer is the fallback. Network steps
(GitHub) are retried with backoff before a run gives up.

Log: ~/.cache/tessera-release.log (cargo's own output: ~/tessera-release/logs).
Status: ~/.cache/tessera-release.json: state (idle, building, ready, failed),
target, tree, commit, step, progress, started, finished, checked, error, ready
(the sets waiting), and per target the last result. One run at a time (flock).
"""
import argparse
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.request

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
ROOT = os.environ.get("TESSERA_RELEASE_ROOT") or os.path.join(HOME, "tessera-release")
SRC = os.path.join(ROOT, "src")
OUT = os.path.join(ROOT, "out")
# What a set's READY can hold (its "format"): 1 archives and the manifest,
# 2 patches and bundles too. The laptop's publisher refuses a set newer
# than it knows and says to reinstall it (audit #9: an older copy refused
# every set, one at a time, for days)
SET_FORMAT = 2
# Nothing else watches the publisher (audit #8): a set READY this long is
# said once through ALERT_HOOK (any program: mail, ntfy… its arguments a
# title and a body), and always in the log
STALL_HOURS = 6
ALERT_HOOK = os.environ.get("TESSERA_RELEASE_ALERT") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), "bin", "tessera-release-alert")
BUILT = os.path.join(ROOT, "built")
TARGETS = os.path.join(ROOT, "target")
LOGS = os.path.join(ROOT, "logs")
CACHE = os.path.join(HOME, ".cache")
LOG = os.path.join(CACHE, "tessera-release.log")
STATUS = os.path.join(CACHE, "tessera-release.json")
TBUILD = os.path.join(HOME, "bin", "tbuild")

REPO_URL = os.environ.get("TESSERA_RELEASE_URL") or "https://github.com/monishbl/tessera.git"
GH_REPO = os.environ.get("TESSERA_RELEASE_GH_REPO") or "monishbl/tessera"
# branch → (channel, rolling release), as the workflow names them
BRANCHES = {"main": ("stable", "tessera-ui-latest"), "beta": ("beta", "tessera-ui-beta")}
VARIANTS = (("x86-64-v3", "-C target-cpu=x86-64-v3"), ("generic", ""))
PARALLEL_RAM = 24 * 1024 ** 3  # both variants at once only with this much memory (two links)


def profile_for(channel):
    """beta: "local" (thin LTO, minutes); stable and tags: "release" (full LTO)"""
    return "local" if channel == "beta" else "release"


def mem_total(meminfo=None):
    """MemTotal in bytes (0 when it can't tell)"""
    try:
        text = meminfo if meminfo is not None else open("/proc/meminfo").read()
    except OSError:
        return 0
    m = re.search(r"^MemTotal:\s+(\d+)\s*kB", text, re.M)
    return int(m.group(1)) * 1024 if m else 0


def linker_flags(which=shutil.which):
    """mold, when it's installed: much faster links (the release profile's
    LTO link most of all)"""
    return "-C link-arg=-fuse-ld=mold" if which("mold") else ""


def with_flags(rustflags, extra):
    return " ".join(x for x in (rustflags, extra) if x)
KEEP_PUBLISHED = 3  # published sets kept here per release
PATCH_FROM = 3  # patches from this many earlier published builds of the release
PATCH_LEVEL = 19
PATCH_WINDOW = 28  # zstd --long (tools/native-install.py's PATCH_WINDOW: the same)
PRETEST = os.environ.get("TESSERA_PRETEST") or os.path.join(HOME, "bin", "tessera-pretest")
PATCH_RE = re.compile(r"^tessera-ui-([0-9a-f]{40})-(x86-64-v3|generic)\.(tessera-ui|tessera-events)\.from-([0-9a-f]{12})\.zst$")
KEEP_BUILT = 6  # built trees kept in built/
TREE_HEX = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{40}$")
# built/<tree>-<channel> (built/<tree> alone: from before channels were kept apart)
BUILT_RE = re.compile(r"^([0-9a-f]{40})(?:-([a-z]+))?$")
TAG_RE = re.compile(r"^v[0-9A-Za-z._-]+$")


class Stop(Exception):
    """This target can't go on; the message says why and what to do."""


# ── Log and status ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def now():
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z")


def log(msg):
    line = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S ") + msg
    print(line, flush=True)
    os.makedirs(CACHE, exist_ok=True)
    try:
        if os.path.getsize(LOG) > 4 << 20:
            os.replace(LOG, LOG + ".1")
    except OSError:
        pass
    with open(LOG, "a") as f:
        f.write(line + "\n")


def load_status():
    try:
        with open(STATUS) as f:
            s = json.load(f)
            return s if isinstance(s, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


STATE = load_status()


import threading
_LOCK = threading.Lock()  # (the two variants build at once)


def status(_target=None, **kw):
    """KW (and one target's result) into the status file. Read again and
    written under one lock: a build and --mark-published (another process,
    its STATE loaded long before) never undo each other's changes, and
    each writes its own temp file."""
    with _LOCK:
        os.makedirs(CACHE, exist_ok=True)
        with open(STATUS + ".lock", "w") as lk:
            fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            cur = load_status()
            cur.update(kw)
            if _target:
                cur.setdefault("targets", {})[_target[0]] = _target[1]
            cur["updated"] = now()
            STATE.clear()
            STATE.update(cur)
            tmp = f"{STATUS}.tmp-{os.getpid()}"
            with open(tmp, "w") as f:
                json.dump(STATE, f, indent=2)
                f.write("\n")
            os.replace(tmp, STATUS)


def target_result(name, **kw):
    status(_target=(name, dict(kw, at=now())))


# ── Helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def run(cmd, *, cwd=None, env=None, check=True, timeout=None):
    # (a hang is a failure like any other: recorded, and with_retries tries
    # again; it ended the run in a traceback with the status left "idle,
    # fetching"; audit #81)
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, env=env, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise Stop(f"{os.path.basename(cmd[0])} {' '.join(cmd[1:3])} timed out after {timeout} s") from None
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        raise Stop(f"{os.path.basename(cmd[0])} {' '.join(cmd[1:3])} failed: "
                   + (r.stderr.strip().splitlines() or ["exit " + str(r.returncode)])[-1])
    return r


def git(*args, check=True):
    r = run(["git", "-C", SRC, *args], check=check, timeout=600)
    return r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else None


def sha256_of(path):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        for block in iter(lambda: f.read(1 << 20), b""):
            h.update(block)
    return h.hexdigest()


def no_display_env():
    return {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items()
            if k not in ("WAYLAND_DISPLAY", "WAYLAND_SOCKET", "DISPLAY", "HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE")}


def with_retries(what, fn, tries=4, waits=(5, 20, 60)):
    """FN, again after a pause when it fails for the network (Stop with
    "can't be reached" or a 5xx): 5 s, 20 s, 60 s, then it gives up"""
    for i in range(tries):
        try:
            return fn()
        except Stop as e:
            transient = any(w in str(e) for w in ("can't be reached", "answered 5", "timed out", "Could not resolve", "Connection"))
            if not transient or i == tries - 1:
                raise
            log(f"{what}: {e}; trying again in {waits[min(i, len(waits) - 1)]} s")
            time.sleep(waits[min(i, len(waits) - 1)])


def published_on_github(tag, tree):
    """Is the tree's manifest in that release? Asked anonymously (the
    repository is public): True / False; raises Stop when GitHub can't be
    reached."""
    url = f"https://github.com/{GH_REPO}/releases/download/{tag}/tessera-ui-{tree}.manifest.json"
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, method="HEAD", headers={"User-Agent": "tessera-release"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            return r.status == 200
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        if e.code in (404, 410):
            return False
        raise Stop(f"GitHub answered {e.code} for {url}") from None
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as e:
        raise Stop(f"GitHub can't be reached ({e})") from None


def write_json(path, obj):
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


# ── Sources ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def fetch_sources(branches, tags):
    os.makedirs(ROOT, exist_ok=True)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(SRC, ".git")):
        shutil.rmtree(SRC, ignore_errors=True)
        log(f"cloning {REPO_URL} into {SRC}")
        run(["git", "clone", "--quiet", "--no-checkout", REPO_URL, SRC], timeout=1800)
    git("remote", "set-url", "origin", REPO_URL)
    specs = [f"+refs/heads/{b}:refs/remotes/origin/{b}" for b in branches]
    if tags:
        specs.append("+refs/tags/v*:refs/tags/v*")
    with_retries("fetching from GitHub", lambda: git("fetch", "--quiet", "--prune", "--no-tags", "origin", *specs))


def targets(branches, tags):
    """What to build: [{name, kind, tag, channel, commit}], branches first."""
    out = []
    for b in branches:
        commit = git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", f"refs/remotes/origin/{b}^{{commit}}", check=False)
        if commit:
            channel, tag = BRANCHES[b]
            out.append({"name": b, "kind": "branch", "tag": tag, "channel": channel, "commit": commit})
    if tags:
        for t in (git("tag", "--list", "v*") or "").split():
            if TAG_RE.match(t):
                commit = git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", f"refs/tags/{t}^{{commit}}", check=False)
                if commit:
                    out.append({"name": t, "kind": "tag", "tag": t, "channel": "release", "commit": commit})
    return out


def checkout(commit):
    git("checkout", "--quiet", "--force", "--detach", commit)
    git("clean", "-ffdxq")


# ── Build and pack (as the workflow's build job) ─────────────────────────

def load_counts():
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(ROOT, "counts.json")) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def build_env(t, variant):
    """What the build tells tessera-ui about itself (native/tessera-ui/build.rs:
    `tessera-ui --version`, Settings → About): the channel (stable, beta, or
    release for a tag), the variant, that it's a release, and the commit and
    its date (so they don't depend on the clone's state)."""
    return {"TESSERA_BUILD_CHANNEL": t["channel"], "TESSERA_BUILD_VARIANT": variant, "TESSERA_BUILD_KIND": "release",
            "TESSERA_BUILD_COMMIT": t["commit"],
            "TESSERA_BUILD_DATE": git("log", "-1", "--format=%cs", t["commit"], check=False) or ""}


def cargo(args, variant, rustflags, label, logf, extra=None):
    """~/bin/tbuild cargo ARGS for VARIANT, its output to LOGF, the count of
    crates compiled in the status ("about": the last build's count). EXTRA:
    more environment (build_env)."""
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items()
           if k not in ("CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS", "RUSTC_WRAPPER", "RUSTC_WORKSPACE_WRAPPER",
                        "CARGO_BUILD_RUSTFLAGS", "CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO")}
    env.update(RUSTFLAGS=rustflags, CARGO_INCREMENTAL="0", CARGO_TERM_COLOR="never",
               CARGO_TARGET_DIR=os.path.join(TARGETS, variant), TBUILD_URGENT="")
    env.update(extra or {})
    counts = load_counts()
    key = f"{variant}:{label}"
    about = counts.get(key)
    done = 0
    last_write = 0
    logf.write(f"\n== {now()} {label} ({variant}) RUSTFLAGS={rustflags!r}"
               + "".join(f" {k}={v}" for k, v in sorted((extra or {}).items())) + "\n")
    logf.flush()
    p = subprocess.Popen([TBUILD, *args], cwd=SRC, env=env, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                         text=True, errors="replace")
    tail = []
    for line in p.stdout:
        logf.write(line)
        tail = (tail + [line.rstrip()])[-30:]
        if line.lstrip().startswith("Compiling "):
            done += 1
            if time.time() - last_write > 3:
                last_write = time.time()
                status(progress={"done": done, "about": about}, step=f"{variant}: {label} ({line.split()[1]})")
    code = p.wait()
    logf.flush()
    if code != 0:
        for t in tail[-12:]:
            log("  | " + t)
        raise Stop(f"the {variant} build of {label} failed (exit {code}); cargo's output: {logf.name}")
    if done:
        with _LOCK:
            counts = load_counts()
            counts[key] = done
            write_json(os.path.join(ROOT, "counts.json"), counts)
    status(progress={"done": done, "about": about}, step=f"{variant}: {label} linked")


def built_dir(tree, channel):
    """Where TREE's programs built for CHANNEL are kept: one folder per
    channel, never shared (the programs carry the channel; audit #725)"""
    if not TREE_HEX.match(tree or "") or not re.match(r"^[a-z]+$", channel or ""):
        raise Stop(f"no build folder for tree {tree!r} on channel {channel!r}")
    return os.path.join(BUILT, f"{tree}-{channel}")


def variant_ok(outdir, variant, profile=None):
    """The packed variant in OUTDIR when it's whole (and, given PROFILE
    "release", built with the release profile: a beta build isn't packed for
    main; any build will do for beta)"""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(outdir, f"variant-{variant}.json")) as f:
            v = json.load(f)
        path = os.path.join(outdir, v["file"])
        if profile == "release" and v.get("profile", "release") != "release":
            return None
        return v if os.path.getsize(path) == v["size"] and sha256_of(path) == v["sha256"] else None
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return None


def build(t, tree):
    """Both variants of TREE in built/<tree>-<channel> (kept from an earlier
    run for the same channel when they're there and whole). Returns
    {variant: variant-json}."""
    outdir = built_dir(tree, t["channel"])
    os.makedirs(outdir, exist_ok=True)
    os.makedirs(LOGS, exist_ok=True)
    epoch = git("log", "-1", "--format=%ct", t["commit"])
    got = {}

    profile = profile_for(t["channel"])
    link = linker_flags()

    def one(variant, rustflags):
        status(state="building", step=f"{variant}: starting", progress=None)
        t0 = time.time()
        prof = ["--release"] if profile == "release" else ["--profile", profile]
        flags = with_flags(rustflags, link)
        with open(os.path.join(LOGS, f"{tree[:12]}-{variant}.log"), "a") as logf:
            cargo(["build", *prof, "--locked", "--manifest-path", "native/tessera-ui/Cargo.toml", "--bin", "tessera-ui"],
                  variant, flags, "tessera-ui", logf, build_env(t, variant))
            cargo(["build", *prof, "--locked", "--manifest-path", "native/tessera-events/Cargo.toml"],
                  variant, flags, "tessera-events", logf)
        status(step=f"{variant}: packing", progress=None)
        v = pack(outdir, tree, variant, epoch, profile)
        log(f"{t['name']}: built {variant} in {int(time.time() - t0)} s ({v['size']} bytes)")
        return v

    # Both variants at once (each its own target folder): one after the
    # other took about 33 minutes, most of it each one's link, and a push
    # waited that long for its ready-made build (19 Nov)
    todo = []
    for variant, rustflags in VARIANTS:
        v = variant_ok(outdir, variant, profile)
        if v:
            got[variant] = v
        else:
            todo.append((variant, rustflags))
    if todo:
        from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor
        # (at once only with the memory for two links; else one after the other)
        workers = len(todo) if mem_total() >= PARALLEL_RAM else 1
        with ThreadPoolExecutor(workers) as ex:
            futs = {variant: ex.submit(one, variant, rustflags) for variant, rustflags in todo}
            for variant, f in futs.items():
                got[variant] = f.result()  # (a failed one raises Stop, as before)
    os.utime(outdir)
    return got


def pack(outdir, tree, variant, epoch, profile="release"):
    """As the workflow's Pack step: both programs in a reproducible
    tar.zst, and variant-<variant>.json describing it."""
    rel = os.path.join(TARGETS, variant, profile)
    stage = os.path.join(outdir, f".stage-{variant}")
    shutil.rmtree(stage, ignore_errors=True)
    os.makedirs(stage)
    versions = {}
    names = ["tessera-ui", "tessera-events"]
    for name in names:
        shutil.copy2(os.path.join(rel, name), os.path.join(stage, name))
        # (--version only, and never with a display)
        versions[name] = run([os.path.join(stage, name), "--version"], env=no_display_env(), timeout=30).stdout.strip()
    file = f"tessera-ui-{tree}-{variant}.tar.zst"
    dest = os.path.join(outdir, file)
    tmp = dest + ".tmp"
    tar = subprocess.Popen(["tar", "--sort=name", "--owner=0", "--group=0", "--numeric-owner", f"--mtime=@{epoch}",
                            "-C", stage, "-cf", "-", *names], stdout=subprocess.PIPE)
    z = subprocess.run(["nice", "-n", "10", "zstd", "-q", "-19", "-T0", "-f", "-o", tmp], stdin=tar.stdout)
    tar.stdout.close()
    if tar.wait() != 0 or z.returncode != 0:
        raise Stop(f"packing {file} failed")
    os.replace(tmp, dest)
    v = {"file": file, "sha256": sha256_of(dest), "size": os.path.getsize(dest), "profile": profile,
         "programs": {name: {"sha256": sha256_of(os.path.join(stage, name)), "version": versions[name]}
                      for name in names}}
    write_json(os.path.join(outdir, f"variant-{variant}.json"), v)
    shutil.rmtree(stage, ignore_errors=True)
    return v


# ── Tested before it's offered ───────────────────────────────────────────

def pretest(tree, variants, channel):
    """Each variant's tessera-ui in a sandbox arena (pretest.sh): it must
    start, answer, draw, lock and unlock. Raises Stop with why."""
    if os.environ.get("TESSERA_RELEASE_NO_PRETEST") == "1":
        return
    if not os.path.exists(PRETEST):
        raise Stop(f"the test before publishing isn't installed ({PRETEST}): run tools/release-builder/install.sh")
    for variant, v in variants.items():
        status(step=f"{variant}: testing in a sandbox", progress=None)
        work = os.path.join(ROOT, "pretest", variant)
        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
        os.makedirs(work)
        unpack_programs(os.path.join(built_dir(tree, channel), v["file"]), work)
        r = subprocess.run([PRETEST, os.path.join(work, "tessera-ui"), SRC, "71" if variant == "x86-64-v3" else "72"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=600)
        last = (r.stdout.strip().splitlines() or ["no answer"])[-1]
        log(f"tree {tree[:12]} {variant}: {last}")
        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            raise Stop(f"the {variant} build failed its test before publishing: {last}")


def unpack_programs(tarball, into):
    """Both programs of a packed variant into INTO"""
    tar = subprocess.Popen(["zstd", "-q", "-d", "-c", tarball], stdout=subprocess.PIPE)
    r = subprocess.run(["tar", "-x", "-C", into], stdin=tar.stdout, capture_output=True)
    tar.stdout.close()
    if tar.wait() != 0 or r.returncode != 0:
        raise Stop(f"unpacking {os.path.basename(tarball)} failed")


# ── Patches from the builds before ───────────────────────────────────────

def earlier_trees(tag, tree, channel):
    """The last PATCH_FROM builds published in TAG (newest first) whose
    archives are still kept here, built for CHANNEL: the programs that
    channel's installs have (a patch from another channel's build never
    applies; audit #725)"""
    out = []
    for _, _, _, info in sorted(sets("PUBLISHED"), key=lambda s: s[3].get("published", ""), reverse=True):
        old = info.get("tree")
        if info.get("type") == "bundle" or info.get("tag") != tag or old == tree or old in out:
            continue
        if info.get("channel", channel) != channel or not TREE_HEX.match(old or ""):
            continue
        if all(variant_ok(built_dir(old, channel), v) for v, _ in VARIANTS):
            out.append(old)
        if len(out) == PATCH_FROM:
            break
    return out


def make_patches(tag, tree, variants, dest, channel):
    """Patches into DEST from each earlier build to this one (the same
    channel's); each variant's manifest entry gets "patches": {from tree:
    {program: {file, size, sha256, from_sha256}}}. Returns the patch files' names."""
    names = []
    olds = earlier_trees(tag, tree, channel)
    if not olds:
        return names
    work = os.path.join(ROOT, "patching")
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    for variant, v in variants.items():
        new_dir = os.path.join(work, "new-" + variant)
        os.makedirs(new_dir)
        unpack_programs(os.path.join(built_dir(tree, channel), v["file"]), new_dir)
        entry = {}
        for old in olds:
            ov = variant_ok(built_dir(old, channel), variant)
            old_dir = os.path.join(work, old[:12] + "-" + variant)
            os.makedirs(old_dir, exist_ok=True)
            unpack_programs(os.path.join(built_dir(old, channel), ov["file"]), old_dir)
            for prog in ("tessera-ui", "tessera-events"):
                a, b = os.path.join(old_dir, prog), os.path.join(new_dir, prog)
                fa, fb = sha256_of(a), sha256_of(b)
                if fa == fb:
                    continue  # (the same program: an install keeps it, nothing to download)
                name = f"tessera-ui-{tree}-{variant}.{prog}.from-{old[:12]}.zst"
                status(step=f"{variant}: patch from {old[:12]} ({prog})", progress=None)
                r = subprocess.run(["nice", "-n", "10", "zstd", "-q", "-f", f"-{PATCH_LEVEL}", f"--long={PATCH_WINDOW}",
                                    f"--patch-from={a}", b, "-o", os.path.join(dest, name)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=1800)
                if r.returncode != 0:
                    log(f"patch {name} failed (skipped): {r.stderr.strip()[-200:]}")
                    continue
                pth = os.path.join(dest, name)
                entry.setdefault(old, {})[prog] = {"file": name, "size": os.path.getsize(pth), "sha256": sha256_of(pth), "from_sha256": fa}
                names.append(name)
            shutil.rmtree(old_dir, ignore_errors=True)
        if entry:
            v["patches"] = entry
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    if names:
        log(f"tree {tree[:12]}: {len(names)} patches from {', '.join(o[:12] for o in olds)} "
            f"({sum(os.path.getsize(os.path.join(dest, n)) for n in names)} bytes)")
    return names


# ── The set for the laptop (unsigned: the laptop signs) ──────────────────

def make_set(t, tree, variants):
    """Both archives and the manifest (as the workflow writes it) in
    out/<tag>/<tree>/, READY written last. Nothing is signed here."""
    commit, tag = t["commit"], t["tag"]
    built = built_dir(tree, t["channel"])
    dest = os.path.join(OUT, tag, tree)
    shutil.rmtree(dest, ignore_errors=True)
    os.makedirs(dest)
    for v in variants.values():
        os.link(os.path.join(built, v["file"]), os.path.join(dest, v["file"]))
    variants = {k: dict(v) for k, v in variants.items()}
    patches = make_patches(tag, tree, variants, dest, t["channel"])
    with open(os.path.join(SRC, "native", "tessera-ui", "Cargo.toml")) as f:
        version = next((m[1] for m in (re.match(r'^version = "(.*)"$', l.rstrip("\n")) for l in f) if m), "")
    manifest = {"format": 1, "name": "tessera-ui", "commit": commit, "tree": tree, "version": version,
                "channel": t["channel"], "tag": tag, "built": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()),
                "variants": {"x86-64-v3": variants["x86-64-v3"], "generic": variants["generic"]}}
    write_json(os.path.join(dest, f"tessera-ui-{tree}.manifest.json"), manifest)
    files = {n: {"size": os.path.getsize(os.path.join(dest, n)), "sha256": sha256_of(os.path.join(dest, n))}
             for n in sorted(os.listdir(dest))}
    ready = {"format": SET_FORMAT, "name": t["name"], "kind": t["kind"], "tag": tag, "channel": t["channel"], "tree": tree,
             "commit": commit, "version": version, "ready": now(), "files": files, "patches": sorted(patches)}
    write_json(os.path.join(dest, "READY"), ready)
    log(f"{t['name']}: ready for the laptop to sign and publish: {dest}")
    return ready


# ── Bundles (one per commit: tools/tessera-bundle.py) ────────────────────

def published_bundle(tag, commit):
    """Is the commit's bundle manifest in that release? (as published_on_github)"""
    url = f"https://github.com/{GH_REPO}/releases/download/{tag}/tessera-{commit}.bundle.json"
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, method="HEAD", headers={"User-Agent": "tessera-release"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            return r.status == 200
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        if e.code in (404, 410):
            return False
        raise Stop(f"GitHub answered {e.code} for {url}") from None
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as e:
        raise Stop(f"GitHub can't be reached ({e})") from None


def load_packer():
    """The commit's own tools/tessera-bundle.py (in the clone, checked out)"""
    import importlib.machinery
    import importlib.util
    path = os.path.join(SRC, "tools", "tessera-bundle.py")
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("tessera_bundle_packer", path)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("tessera_bundle_packer", loader)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


PARTS = (("shaders", ["tools/build-shaders.sh"], {}), ("native helpers", ["shell/native/build.sh"], {}),
         ("glass plugin", ["bash", "tools/build-plugin.sh"], None))


def build_parts(plugin_dir, logf):
    """The shaders, native helpers and glass plugin, built in the clone (the
    plugin into PLUGIN_DIR, against this machine's Hyprland). Raises Stop."""
    for what, cmd, env in PARTS:
        status(step=f"bundle: {what}", progress=None)
        e = dict(os.environ, TESSERA_PLUGIN_DEST=plugin_dir) if env is None else dict(os.environ)
        e.pop("TESSERA_PROGRESS_TTY", None)
        cmd = [os.path.join(SRC, cmd[0])] + cmd[1:] if not cmd[0] == "bash" else ["bash", os.path.join(SRC, cmd[1])]
        logf.write(f"\n== {now()} {what}\n")
        logf.flush()
        r = subprocess.run(["nice", "-n", "10", *cmd], cwd=SRC, env=e, stdout=logf, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, timeout=3600)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            raise Stop(f"the bundle's {what} didn't build (exit {r.returncode}); its output: {logf.name}")


def make_bundle(t, tree, variants):
    """The commit's bundle, both variants, and its manifest, in
    out/<tag>/<commit>/ with READY ("type": "bundle") written last.
    VARIANTS: the programs' packed variants (built/<tree>-<channel>). Unsigned."""
    commit, tag = t["commit"], t["tag"]
    dest = os.path.join(OUT, tag, commit)
    shutil.rmtree(dest, ignore_errors=True)
    os.makedirs(dest)
    work = os.path.join(ROOT, "bundling")
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    os.makedirs(work)
    try:
        B = load_packer()
        plugin = os.path.join(work, "plugin")
        os.makedirs(plugin)
        os.makedirs(LOGS, exist_ok=True)
        with open(os.path.join(LOGS, f"bundle-{commit[:12]}.log"), "a") as logf:
            build_parts(plugin, logf)
        epoch = int(git("log", "-1", "--format=%ct", commit) or 0)
        entries = {}
        for variant, v in variants.items():
            status(step=f"bundle: packing {variant}", progress=None)
            progs = os.path.join(work, "programs-" + variant)
            os.makedirs(progs)
            unpack_programs(os.path.join(built_dir(tree, t["channel"]), v["file"]), progs)
            entries[variant] = B.pack_variant(SRC, commit, variant, {n: os.path.join(progs, n) for n in ("tessera-ui", "tessera-events")},
                                              plugin, dest, epoch)
        with open(os.path.join(SRC, "native", "tessera-ui", "Cargo.toml")) as f:
            version = next((m[1] for m in (re.match(r'^version = "(.*)"$', l.rstrip("\n")) for l in f) if m), "")
        lock = B.system_lock()
        m = B.make_manifest(SRC, commit, t["channel"], entries, lock, tree=tree, tag=tag, version=version)
        write_json(os.path.join(dest, B.manifest_name(commit)), m)
    except Exception as e:
        shutil.rmtree(dest, ignore_errors=True)
        raise Stop(f"the bundle couldn't be made: {getattr(e, 'why', None) or e}") from None
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    files = {n: {"size": os.path.getsize(os.path.join(dest, n)), "sha256": sha256_of(os.path.join(dest, n))}
             for n in sorted(os.listdir(dest))}
    ready = {"format": SET_FORMAT, "type": "bundle", "name": t["name"], "kind": t["kind"], "tag": tag, "channel": t["channel"], "tree": tree,
             "commit": commit, "version": version, "ready": now(), "files": files, "patches": [],
             "latest": t["kind"] == "branch"}
    write_json(os.path.join(dest, "READY"), ready)
    sizes = ", ".join("%s %d bytes" % (v, e["size"]) for v, e in entries.items())
    held = ", ".join(m["packages"]["held"]) or "none"
    log(f"{t['name']}: bundle ready for the laptop to sign and publish: {dest} ({sizes}; held: {held})")
    return ready


def do_bundle(t, tree, build_only):
    """The commit's bundle, unless it's ready, published, or the commit has
    no tools/tessera-bundle.py. The programs come from built/<tree>-<channel> (built
    now when they aren't kept)."""
    if os.environ.get("TESSERA_RELEASE_NO_BUNDLE") == "1":
        return
    name, tag, commit = t["name"], t["tag"], t["commit"]
    here = os.path.join(OUT, tag, commit)
    if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(here, "READY")) or os.path.isfile(os.path.join(here, "PUBLISHED")):
        return
    if git("cat-file", "-e", f"{commit}:tools/tessera-bundle.py", check=False) is None:
        return  # (from before bundles)
    if not build_only and with_retries("asking GitHub", lambda: published_bundle(tag, commit)):
        return
    # (a bundle that failed for this commit waits before it's made again:
    # 10 min, 1 h, then 6 h; it was rebuilt, minutes of CPU, every run;
    # audit #82. A new commit tries at once)
    prev = STATE.get("targets", {}).get(name + ":bundle") or {}
    if prev.get("result") == "failed" and prev.get("commit") == commit:
        wait = (600, 3600, 6 * 3600)[min(prev.get("fails", 1), 3) - 1]
        if time.time() - prev.get("t", 0) < wait:
            raise Stop(prev.get("why") or "the bundle failed")
    status(state="building", step="bundle: preparing", progress=None)
    try:
        checkout(commit)
        variants = build(t, tree)
        make_bundle(t, tree, variants)
    except Stop as e:
        fails = prev.get("fails", 0) + 1 if prev.get("commit") == commit else 1
        if prev.get("why") != f"bundle: {e}":
            log(f"failed: {name}: bundle: {e}")
        target_result(name + ":bundle", result="failed", tag=tag, commit=commit, why=f"bundle: {e}", fails=fails, t=time.time())
        raise Stop(f"bundle: {e}") from None
    target_result(name + ":bundle", result="ready", tag=tag, commit=commit, dir=here)


# ── Sets for the laptop ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

def sets(kind="READY"):
    """[(tag, tree, path, info)] of the sets with that marker."""
    out = []
    try:
        tags = os.listdir(OUT)
    except OSError:
        return out
    for tag in tags:
        tdir = os.path.join(OUT, tag)
        if not os.path.isdir(tdir) or not (TAG_RE.match(tag) or tag in ("tessera-ui-latest", "tessera-ui-beta")):
            continue
        for tree in os.listdir(tdir):
            marker = os.path.join(tdir, tree, kind)
            if TREE_HEX.match(tree) and os.path.isfile(marker):
                try:
                    with open(marker) as f:
                        info = json.load(f)
                except (OSError, ValueError):
                    continue
                out.append((tag, tree, os.path.join(tdir, tree), info))
    return out


def list_ready():
    return [dict(info, dir=path) for _, _, path, info in sorted(sets(), key=lambda s: s[3].get("ready", ""))]


def alert_stalled(now_t=None, run=subprocess.run):
    """Sets READY more than STALL_HOURS: said in the log, and once each
    through ALERT_HOOK when there is one (it isn't the publisher's to say:
    it may not be running at all). Returns the sets said."""
    now_t = time.time() if now_t is None else now_t
    seen_file = os.path.join(ROOT, "alerted.json")
    try:
        with open(seen_file) as f:
            seen = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        seen = {}
    said, waiting = [], set()
    for tag, tree, _, info in sets():
        key = f"{tag}/{tree}"
        waiting.add(key)
        try:
            # (now() is local time, as the publisher reads it too)
            ready_t = time.mktime(time.strptime(str(info.get("ready", ""))[:19], "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"))
        except (ValueError, OverflowError):
            continue
        hours = (now_t - ready_t) / 3600
        if hours < STALL_HOURS or key in seen:
            continue
        body = (f"{info.get('name', tag)} ({tree[:12]}) has waited {int(hours)} h to be signed and published. "
                f"Is tessera-publish.timer running on the signing laptop (tools/release-builder/install-publisher.sh), with its signing key?")
        log(f"stalled: {body}")
        if os.access(ALERT_HOOK, os.X_OK):
            try:
                run([ALERT_HOOK, "A Tessera release is stuck", body], capture_output=True, timeout=60)
            except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
                log(f"stalled: {ALERT_HOOK} failed: {e}")
        seen[key] = now()
        said.append(key)
    seen = {k: v for k, v in seen.items() if k in waiting}
    write_json(seen_file, seen)
    return said


def mark_published(tag, tree):
    path = os.path.join(OUT, tag, tree)
    if not (TREE_HEX.match(tree) and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(path, "READY"))):
        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(path, "PUBLISHED")):
            return 0
        print(f"tessera-release: there's no ready set {tag}/{tree}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    with open(os.path.join(path, "READY")) as f:
        info = json.load(f)
    info["published"] = now()
    write_json(os.path.join(path, "PUBLISHED"), info)
    os.remove(os.path.join(path, "READY"))
    log(f"{info.get('name', tag)}: published (tree {tree[:12]} in {tag}), as the laptop says")
    target_result(info.get("name", tag), result="published", tag=tag, tree=tree, commit=info.get("commit"))
    waiting = [f"{t}/{tr}" for t, tr, _, _ in sets()]
    if STATE.get("state") in ("ready", "idle"):
        status(state="ready" if waiting else "idle", ready=waiting)
    else:
        status(ready=waiting)
    return 0


def prune():
    # (published sets: the newest three per release; built trees: six)
    by_tag = {}
    for tag, tree, path, info in sets("PUBLISHED"):
        # (bundles and program sets kept apart: the newest three of each)
        by_tag.setdefault((tag, info.get("type", "programs")), []).append((info.get("published", ""), path))
    for items in by_tag.values():
        for _, path in sorted(items, reverse=True)[KEEP_PUBLISHED:]:
            shutil.rmtree(path, ignore_errors=True)
    try:
        trees = sorted((d for d in os.listdir(BUILT) if BUILT_RE.match(d)),
                       key=lambda d: os.path.getmtime(os.path.join(BUILT, d)), reverse=True)
    except OSError:
        return
    waiting = {info.get("tree") or tree for _, tree, _, info in sets()}
    for d in trees[KEEP_BUILT:]:
        # (built/<tree>-<channel>; an old built/<tree> is never used again: it goes in turn)
        if BUILT_RE.match(d).group(1) in waiting:
            continue
        shutil.rmtree(os.path.join(BUILT, d), ignore_errors=True)
        for v, _ in VARIANTS:
            try:
                os.remove(os.path.join(LOGS, f"{d[:12]}-{v}.log"))
            except OSError:
                pass


# ── A run ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def do_target(t, build_only):
    tree = programs_target(t, build_only)
    if tree:
        do_bundle(t, tree, build_only)


def programs_target(t, build_only):
    """The program set for the target's native/ tree (as before bundles);
    returns the tree, or None when the commit can't be built from"""
    name, tag, commit = t["name"], t["tag"], t["commit"]
    tree = git("rev-parse", f"{commit}:native")
    prev = STATE.get("targets", {}).get(name) or {}
    status(target=name, commit=commit, tree=tree)
    if git("cat-file", "-e", f"{commit}:tools/tessera-ui.pub", check=False) is None:
        why = f"{name} has no tools/tessera-ui.pub, so nothing built from it could be checked"
        if prev.get("why") != why:
            log(f"{name}: skipped: {why}")
            target_result(name, result="skipped", tree=tree, commit=commit, why=why)
        return None
    here = os.path.join(OUT, tag, tree)
    if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(here, "READY")):
        if prev.get("result") != "ready" or prev.get("tree") != tree:
            target_result(name, result="ready", tag=tag, tree=tree, commit=commit, dir=here)
        return tree
    if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(here, "PUBLISHED")):
        return tree
    if not build_only and with_retries("asking GitHub", lambda: published_on_github(tag, tree)):
        if prev.get("tree") != tree or prev.get("result") not in ("published", "up-to-date"):
            log(f"{name}: tree {tree[:12]} is already published in {tag}")
            target_result(name, result="up-to-date", tag=tag, tree=tree, commit=commit)
        return tree
    t0 = time.time()
    status(state="building", started=now(), finished=None, error=None, step="preparing", progress=None)
    log(f"{name}: tree {tree[:12]} (commit {commit[:12]}) has no build for {tag}: "
        + ("building (build only)" if build_only else "building"))
    checkout(commit)
    variants = build(t, tree)
    if build_only:
        target_result(name, result="built", tree=tree, commit=commit, seconds=int(time.time() - t0))
        return tree
    pretest(tree, variants, t["channel"])
    make_set(t, tree, variants)
    target_result(name, result="ready", tag=tag, tree=tree, commit=commit, dir=here, seconds=int(time.time() - t0))
    return tree


def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument("--branch", action="append", choices=sorted(BRANCHES), help="only this branch (repeatable; no tags)")
    ap.add_argument("--build-only", action="store_true", help="build and pack; don't make a ready set")
    ap.add_argument("--status", action="store_true", help="print the status JSON")
    ap.add_argument("--list-ready", action="store_true", help="the sets waiting to be signed and published, as JSON")
    ap.add_argument("--health", action="store_true", help="the sets waiting and the status, in one answer (the laptop's look)")
    ap.add_argument("--mark-published", nargs=2, metavar=("TAG", "TREE"), help="the laptop published this set")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if a.status:
        print(json.dumps(load_status(), indent=2))
        return 0
    if a.health:
        print(json.dumps({"ready": list_ready(), "status": load_status()}, indent=2))
        return 0
    if a.list_ready:
        print(json.dumps(list_ready(), indent=2))
        return 0
    os.makedirs(ROOT, exist_ok=True)
    if a.mark_published:
        # (its own short lock: never waits for a build)
        with open(os.path.join(ROOT, "mark.lock"), "w") as ml:
            fcntl.flock(ml, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
            return mark_published(*a.mark_published)
    lock = open(os.path.join(ROOT, "lock"), "w")
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except BlockingIOError:
        print("tessera-release: another run is going", file=sys.stderr)
        return 0
    branches = a.branch or ["main", "beta"]
    with_tags = not a.branch
    status(pid=os.getpid(), state="idle", step="fetching", progress=None, error=None)
    failed = []
    try:
        fetch_sources(branches, with_tags)
        todo = targets(branches, with_tags)
    except Exception as e:  # (Stop, or an unexpected one: never a traceback with the status left as it was)
        msg = str(e) if isinstance(e, Stop) else f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}"
        log(f"failed: {msg}")
        status(state="failed", error=msg, checked=now(), step=None, pid=None)
        return 1
    for t in todo:
        try:
            do_target(t, a.build_only)
        except Stop as e:
            prev = STATE.get("targets", {}).get(t["name"]) or {}
            bundle = STATE.get("targets", {}).get(t["name"] + ":bundle") or {}
            if str(e) not in (prev.get("why"), bundle.get("why")):
                log(f"failed: {t['name']}: {e}")
            failed.append(f"{t['name']}: {e}")
            target_result(t["name"], result="failed", tree=STATE.get("tree"), commit=t["commit"], why=str(e))
        except Exception as e:  # (an unexpected one: still recorded, never silent)
            msg = f"{t['name']}: {type(e).__name__}: {e}"
            log("failed: " + msg)
            failed.append(msg)
            target_result(t["name"], result="failed", why=msg)
    prune()
    alert_stalled()
    # (finished: when the last build ended; checked: every run)
    end = {"checked": now(), "step": None, "progress": None, "pid": None, "ready": [f"{t}/{tr}" for t, tr, _, _ in sets()]}
    if STATE.get("state") != "idle":
        end["finished"] = end["checked"]
    if failed:
        status(state="failed", error="; ".join(failed), **end)
        return 1
    status(state="ready" if end["ready"] else "idle", error=None, **end)
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
